## Context

Part of the task contract spec (#1675): one record on Dev 5001 that firstmate, every worker and every assistance write and read, shown on the Firstmate board. The spec holds the model (tables, templates, states, events, delivery, owner items, grants) and the order; this is step 7 of 8 (T6).

## Requirements

On a draft copy of `firstmate.board`, then the live row with a pre-image:
- Read the tables with their generated operations in the owner's session, as the page already does for `push_subscription`.
- Board columns are the five steps of the task (Queued, Working, PR, On Dev, Passed; change 199, Step 2), and cards show the stepper, the worker and reviewer, the age in the step, the due marker, the next actor and the block kind.
- The detail tabs are Overview, Timeline (replacing Thread and Activity), Checks (replacing Subtasks) and Plan (unchanged).
- His answers, passes, fails and approvals go through one published writer operation: an API Builder script row on 5001 that runs `bin/fm-task.sh` with the signed-in owner as actor, so the one writer keeps `seq`, the transitions and the `fm_task` projection (and `fm_owner_check` for an owner row). The page does not call `createFmTaskEvent` directly: the page grammar cannot compute seq + 1 (`src/frontend/CFW.Shadcn/src/composition/page-graph-values.ts:179`), and an event alone leaves `fm_task` stale (change 194).
- An owner row opens as a checklist item from `fm_owner_check`: the page title as a link to its direct URL (a new tab for a 5001 or Home address; the screen name for the K50), the steps, the data, what he should see, and Pass or Fail with a note.
- Waiting for you lists next actor owner and closes from the stream or refresh.
- A `done` that carries a document (145) shows it in Overview (the newest `done`) and on its Timeline event, with #1566's components (markdown in `markdown`, HTML in the sandboxed `html-document` frame, `sandbox="allow-scripts"`) but not its fixed box. By the owner's direction in task board-doc-card-space (feedback e2832ad3), the document fills the remaining height of the detail with one scroll (no nested scroll box), and Open large is a true fullscreen that covers the whole viewport and closes back. List reads select only `documents($select=id,title,mediaType)`, and the text is read once, when the document opens.
- Golden story at 1440 and 390 first (project rule).

**The document table first (145).** Before the draft row, and not waiting for #1671: publish `fm_event_document` (child `documents` of `fm_task_event`) exactly as the spec's table lists, through the definition API as SysAdmin, and add it to `docs/fm-task-contract/definitions.json` and its README (ten definitions become eleven). This is its own PR, so T4's real run (TR35) can start.

This takes over #168 (Q4 A) and the comments design of #1546 (Q3 A).

**Row surface:** the T1 tables and `fm_event_document` (OData operations); `firstmate-board` stays only for `plan` and images.
**Grant:** none new (the owner's SysAdmin session).

**Start point (firstmate, planner.inbox 136):** the in-app-feedback worker is changing `fm-board.mjs` and the `firstmate.board` row now (#1671). T6 starts from main after #1671 lands: the draft copy is taken from the `firstmate.board` row as #1671 leaves it, and the pre-image is taken then.

Stop lines: every other tab keeps working; no grant change.

## Steps

- [ ] **Step 1: the task contract board (TR51 to TR53, TR55 to TR58; TR56 first, on its own).** As the Requirements above say: on the draft copy of `firstmate.board`, read the record, the detail tabs, the owner's actions through the published writer operation, Waiting for you, and the `done` document.
- [ ] **Step 2: cards by step (change 199; TR50, KB1 to KB6).** The owner's own board is the reference: columns by step, a five-step stepper on each card, a worker and reviewer line, the age in the step, an overdue marker, and filters. Build it on the same draft copy after Step 1.
  - **Fields first (KB1).** Publish five new nullable `fm_task` fields through the definition API as SysAdmin: `stage` (16: `queued`, `working`, `pr`, `dev`, `passed`), `stage_since` (datetime), `last_event_at` (datetime), `last_note` (300) and `reviewer` (64). Add them to `docs/fm-task-contract/definitions.json` and its README. This is its own PR, like TR56, so the writer's projection (huynhtandat223/firstmate#176, Step 5) can fill them.
  - **The step rule (owned by the writer; the page only reads it).** `done` → `passed`. `review` → `dev` when a `deploy` event follows the newest `done`, else `pr`. `running` → `pr` when a `pr` event follows the newest `started` or `changes`, else `working`. `triage`, `todo` and `ready` → `queued`. `blocked` keeps the step it had. `stage_since` is the time of the event that set the current step. `reviewer` is the actor of the newest `check`, `owner-check`, `approved` or `changes` event. `last_note` is the newest event's note (cut to 300).
  - **Columns (TR50).** There are five columns, Queued, Working, PR, On Dev and Passed. The kanban groups by `stage` instead of `state`, and archived tasks are hidden. A blocked task stays in its step, its current dot turns red, and its block-kind badge shows. A triage task shows a "Triage" badge in Queued. At 390, the existing "Lane" select shows one column at a time.
  - **Card (KB2).** Top to bottom:
    - the title, at most 2 lines;
    - "Worker: <assignee> · Reviewer: <reviewer>", where the reviewer is the next actor when it is the Tester or firstmate and `reviewer` is empty, and "—" when there is none;
    - `last_note`, at most 3 lines;
    - the stepper: passed steps get a check, the current step gets the step tone (red when blocked), later steps are empty;
    - a footer with "In this step <relative age of `stage_since`>" on the left and the due marker (KB3) on the right.

    The "Your decision" and block badges, and the Changed dot, stay. A click opens the detail (TR51, unchanged).
  - **Due and overdue (KB3).** Each step has a budget, kept as page constants that firstmate can tune: Working 24 h, PR 12 h, On Dev 24 h. Queued and Passed have no budget. The due time is `stage_since` plus the budget. For a blocked `transient` task, the due time is `hold_until`. Before the due time the card shows "Due HH:mm dd/MM" in the muted tone. After it, the card shows "Overdue HH:mm dd/MM" in the destructive tone and gets a destructive left border.
  - **Filters (KB4).** Two selects sit above the board. "Waiting on" holds All, Worker, Tester, firstmate and You (`next_actor`). "Repository" holds All, then each short repository name (`huynhtandat223/cfw-modules` counts as `cfw-modules`), then "No repository". The total line reads "<n> tasks · columns by step". The page address keeps both filters.
  - **The stepper is a neutral component (KB5).** It is `@cfw/components/stepper`, with `steps: {label, status: done|current|blocked|todo}[]`, rendered as a list with `aria-current="step"` on the current step and each step's label as its accessible name. Search the registries in `components.json` first (vendor workflow); it has its own tests and a catalog story.
  - **Golden story first (KB5).** Update `golden-firstmate-board-record` (story, `.data.json` with at least one card in each step, one blocked, one overdue, one "Your decision" and one long title) on Storybook 5010 at 1440 and 390, and commit its captures. Only then edit the draft row.
  - Stop lines: the detail, Waiting for you and every other tab stay as Step 1 leaves them. No grant change. The page writes nothing new.
- [ ] **Step 3: the live row (TR54) and cleanup (KB6).**

## Definition of done

Done when every user-visible scenario × width passes in the Tester's record on the deployed head, firstmate approves after that record, and the cleanup scenario passes; internal work requires a PR, green CI (or the repo checks where the repo has no CI), and the real run each scenario names.

